<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Deliberately empty. `tauri.conf.json` names this file so a macOS bundle has entitlements to
    sign with, and Warsha needs no hardened-runtime exception to run: the app writes only inside
    its own config directory, spawns no helper that needs a sandbox escape, and reaches the
    daemon it started on loopback. Signing itself stays off until the owner supplies a
    certificate (M9 recorded the signing hooks as present but disabled).
  -->
</dict>
</plist>
